  "verbalization": "Nicotinamide is implicated in the pathogenesis of Beriberi through a series of interconnected metabolic pathways. The evidence suggests that Nicotinamide is linked to Pellagra, which in turn is associated with Inositol and Nicotinyl Alcohol, all of which are involved in the metabolic cascade leading to Beriberi. The final scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, with the most direct link being Nicotinamide → Pellagra → Beriberi, though the indirect pathways through Inositol and Nicotinyl Alcohol also contribute to this connection. The mechanisms involve the role of these compounds in the metabolism of nicotinic acid, potentially affecting cellular function and energy production. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Inositol and Nicotinyl Alcohol in the development of Beriberi, suggesting that Nicotinamide may act as a precursor or modulator in this metabolic process."
